Chapter: DiagXhci
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Diag chapter DiagStage

 We say:

Section: Reading The Census

 Every cell here is written by the ORDINARY USB bring-up (`GopUsb`'s
 `xhci-ctl-census` at `GopUsb.codex:54` and the notes around it), so this row
 touches no device and issues no transfer. It reports what the bring-up the
 bank already performed recorded about itself. That is why it sits after
 `block`: before the medium is opened these cells are all zero and the row
 could only say so.

  dxh-count : Integer -> Integer
  dxh-count (dummy) = xdiag-get 40

  dxh-id : Integer -> Integer
  dxh-id (i) = xdiag-get (xhci-ctl-base + i * 4)

  dxh-loc : Integer -> Integer
  dxh-loc (i) = xdiag-get (xhci-ctl-base + i * 4 + 1)

  dxh-state : Integer -> Integer
  dxh-state (i) = xdiag-get (xhci-ctl-base + i * 4 + 2)

  dxh-found : Integer -> Integer
  dxh-found (i) = xdiag-get (xhci-ctl-base + i * 4 + 3)

  dxh-has-disk : Integer -> Boolean
  dxh-has-disk (i) = bit-and (dxh-found i) 4 /= 0

Section: Rolling Up

  dxh-any-running : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  dxh-any-running (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then False
    else if i >= xhci-ctl-max then False
    else if dxh-state i == xhci-ctl-running then True
    else dxh-any-running (i + 1) n

  dxh-any-disk : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  dxh-any-disk (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then False
    else if i >= xhci-ctl-max then False
    else if dxh-state i == xhci-ctl-running & dxh-has-disk i then True
    else dxh-any-disk (i + 1) n

Section: Text

  dxh-where : Integer -> Text
  dxh-where (loc) = show (bit-shru loc 16) & ":" & show (bit-and (bit-shru loc 8) 255) & "." & show (bit-and loc 7)

  dxh-who : Integer -> Text
  dxh-who (id) = diag-hex4 (bit-shru id 16) & ":" & diag-hex4 (bit-and id 65535)

  dxh-st-name : Integer -> Text
  dxh-st-name (st) =
    if st == xhci-ctl-running then "running"
    else if st == xhci-ctl-failed then "BRINGUP-FAILED"
    else "never-opened"

  dxh-yn : Integer -> Text
  dxh-yn (v) = if v == 0 then "n" else "y"

  dxh-one : Integer -> Text
  dxh-one (i) =
    let f = dxh-found i
    in "ctl" & show i & " " & dxh-who (dxh-id i) & " at " & dxh-where (dxh-loc i)
       & " " & dxh-st-name (dxh-state i)
       & " kbd=" & dxh-yn (bit-and f 1) & " mouse=" & dxh-yn (bit-and f 2) & " disk=" & dxh-yn (bit-and f 4)

  dxh-rows : Integer, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  dxh-rows (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if i >= xhci-ctl-max then acc
    else dxh-rows (i + 1) n (acc & [dxh-one i])

Section: The Endpoint

 `xhci-ep-base` is written when a HID interrupt endpoint is configured
 (`GopXhci.codex:341-346`). Its first word is the configure status; the two
 after it pair the interval the descriptor ASKED for with the one actually
 programmed, which is the pair the keyboard question turns on.

  dxh-ep : Integer -> Text
  dxh-ep (dummy) =
    let st = xdiag-get xhci-ep-base
    in if st == 0 & xdiag-get 47 == 0 then "hid: no interrupt endpoint was configured"
    else let ask = xdiag-get (xhci-ep-base + 1)
    in let got = xdiag-get (xhci-ep-base + 2)
    in "hid: binds=" & show (xdiag-get 47) & " status=" & diag-hex8 st
       & " asked int=" & show (bit-and ask 65535) & " maxpkt=" & show (bit-shru ask 16)
       & " programmed int=" & show (bit-and got 65535) & " maxpkt=" & show (bit-shru got 16)

Section: The Stage

 `none` is DELIBERATELY AMBIGUOUS and the verdict says so out loud. A census
 count of zero is written both by a box with no xHCI controller and by a run
 where the bring-up never happened, and these cells cannot tell those apart.
 Splitting them would need a separate "the census ran" flag, which nothing
 writes today; inventing a distinction the cells do not carry is how a row
 starts lying (L-STATES).

  dxh-states : List Text = ["running", "no-disk", "bringup-failed", "none"]

  dxh-run : DiagCtx -> DiagResult
  dxh-run (c) =
    let n = dxh-count 0
    in let st = if n <= 0 then "none"
                else if dxh-any-disk 0 n then "running"
                else if dxh-any-running 0 n then "no-disk"
                else "bringup-failed"
    in let colour = if st == "running" then diag-col-good
                    else if st == "none" then diag-col-warn
                    else diag-col-bad
    in let g1 = "ctls=" & show n & "  " & dxh-ep 0
    in diag-result st colour ([g1] & dxh-rows 0 n []) ([g1] & dxh-rows 0 n [])
